{{define "description"}}Every City of Livermore department as a bar split by the fund groups that pay for it; open one to see what it spends by category and which funds pay for it, each figure naming the Budget Book page it was read from.{{end -}}
{{define "head-extra"}}
<script type="application/json" id="department-config">{{.ConfigJSON}}</script>{{end -}}
{{template "head" .}}

<header class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1>{{.Title}}</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{.Lede}}</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="department-main">

<section class="department-bars" aria-labelledby="bars-heading">
  <h2 id="bars-heading">Every department</h2>
  <details class="how-to-read" open>
  <summary>How to read this page</summary>
  <p class="department-bars-how">
    Each bar is a department, longest first, on the one scale the longest sets,
    split by the group of funds that pays for it. Click a department, or press
    Enter or Space on it, to open its fund groups and to show below the bars
    where its money comes from and where it goes, each bar naming the Budget
    Book page its figure was read from.
  </p>
  </details>
  <ul class="department-legend" id="department-legend" aria-label="Fund groups, largest across every department first"></ul>
  <ol class="department-list" id="department-list"></ol>
  <p class="department-bars-sum" id="department-bars-sum">
    ◇ A bar's figure is our sum of the department's funding rows in the column,
    not a total the city prints, and each share is ours too: a fund group's part
    of that sum, rounded to a tenth.
  </p>
</section>

<div class="department-view" id="department-view">

<h3 id="department-heading">Choose a department</h3>

{{- /* The two sentences the client chooses between, worded here. Whether a
       department's two blocks tie in a column is Go's declaration, carried
       per year in the config; the client only picks which to print. */}}
<p class="department-tie" id="department-tie"
   data-ties="Both blocks of this department's page add up to the same sum for this year, to the cent, and this site checks that they still do every time it is built."
   data-held="For this year the two blocks do not add up to the same sum, and the project's checks declare why: "></p>

<div class="department-sides">

<section class="sides-side department-side" data-side="funding" aria-labelledby="funding-heading">
  <h4 id="funding-heading">Where its money comes from</h4>
  <p id="funding-says">
    Read from the department's <strong>Department Funding Sources</strong> block,
    the lower half of its page in the Budget Book (pp.85-125): one bar per fund.
    <strong>Each figure is one fund's share</strong> of the department, not its
    whole cost. The General Fund bar is the General Fund's share alone; every other
    bar is a fund the city keeps apart from it, wearing its fund group's colour.
  </p>
  <p id="internal-service-says">
    A fund marked <em>internal service</em> is one the city fills by charging its own
    departments, so the money it pays here was first charged to another department
    and is counted in that department's cost as well.
  </p>
  <p class="sides-total subtle"></p>
  <figure class="sides-figure" hidden></figure>
</section>

<section class="sides-side department-side" data-side="spending" aria-labelledby="spending-heading">
  <h4 id="spending-heading">Where its money goes</h4>
  <p id="spending-says">
    Read from the department's <strong>Expenditures by Category</strong> block, the
    upper half of the same page: what its divisions spend in each spending
    category, whatever fund pays. <strong>Each figure is the whole department's
    cost</strong> in that category, summed over every division the page prints
    under the department.
  </p>
  <p id="transfers-says" hidden>
    <strong>Transfers Out</strong> is money moved to another of the city's own funds,
    not spent on anything, and its bar is hatched. The page prints it inside the
    division's total, so it is inside this side's sum too.
  </p>
  <p class="sides-total subtle"></p>
  <figure class="sides-figure" hidden></figure>
</section>

</div>

</div>

<div class="tooltip" id="tooltip" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>

<details class="how-to-read" open>
<summary>How to read these bars</summary>
<p class="subtle">
  Both sides are drawn on one scale, the longest bar of either filling its track.
  Point at a bar, or focus it, for the pages its figure was read from;
  {{- if .SourcesPath}} the <a href="{{.SourcesPath}}">Sources and data</a> page lists every cited page.
  {{- else}} the Sources list at the foot of this page names every cited page.{{end}}
  A sum marked ◇ adds the cited bars of its side and is ours, not the city's:
  the page prints a department total of its own, which this site has not read as
  a figure, so neither sum is presented as the department's total. A share
  marked ◇ is ours too: one bar as a percentage of its side's sum.
</p>
</details>

{{- template "caveats-line" .CaveatsHere}}

</main>

{{template "footer" .}}

<template id="department-bar"><li class="department-bar"><div class="department-row" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"><span class="department-name"></span><span class="department-track"></span><span class="department-value"></span></div><div class="department-detail" hidden><ul class="department-groups"></ul><a class="department-to-sides" href="#department-heading">Where its money comes from and goes, below the bars</a></div></li></template>
<template id="department-seg"><span class="department-seg"></span></template>
<template id="department-key"><li><span class="department-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="department-key-name"></span></li></template>
<template id="ledger-list"><ol class="ledger-list"></ol></template>
<template id="ledger-row"><li class="bar-row" tabindex="0" role="button"><span class="bar-label"></span><span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill"></span></span><span class="bar-value"></span><span class="bar-share subtle"></span></li></template>
<template id="department-group"><li><span class="department-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="department-group-name"></span><span class="department-group-value"></span><span class="department-group-share"></span></li></template>

<!-- department.js runs nothing on import, so boot() is called here. -->
<script type="module">import { boot } from "./department.js"; boot();</script>
</body>
</html>
